# pyron COSMO vs DEMITRI FIREBALL — the POOL-vs-POOL CONTACT rig (14z-96).
#
# WHY. The hit-class map census (audit_hitclass_map_cost section 3, 14z-93)
# reads ZERO tenant map entries over all 37 hui+pyron rigs — not because the
# thunk is dead but because NO RIG PRODUCES THE EVENT: the sweep is
# POOL-vs-POOL, and a tenant projectile hitting a walking FIGHTER never
# transits the map. 88_hui_plasma_trap_contact's header names the missing
# ingredient: "an opposing PROJECTILE to clash with — not a walking
# fighter". This is that rig: Pyron's EX Cosmo Disruption (the corpus'
# richest pool source, 17-28 type-66 spawns per rig) against Demitri's
# 236+P Chaos Flare fired INTO the cloud from the right.
#
# THE MOVE COSTS A METER STOCK (71_pyron_cosmo's lesson, paid for three
# times before it): with an empty meter the EX pair downgrades and nothing
# fires, so the runner MUST poke the stock count before EVERY attempt.
# POKES (both picks + P1 meter before each attempt):
#   1400:ff8782:11;1450:ff8782:11;1500:ff8782:11;1400:ff8b82:01;1450:ff8b82:01;1500:ff8b82:01;3300:ff8509:03;3320:ff8509:03;4100:ff8509:03;4120:ff8509:03;4900:ff8509:03;4920:ff8509:03
#
# P1 starts LEFT facing right: 41236 = L,DL,D,DR,R then hold/release 45
# (2K). P2 starts RIGHT facing left: 236 = D,DL,L; button 1 = LP. Fireball
# timing brackets the cosmo release (~f+55 after the motion) so at least
# one flare is IN FLIGHT while the cloud is live; two more follow because
# the flare's travel time is unmeasured. INPUT GRAMMAR, paid for in v1:
# the punch must OVERLAP the final direction (p2=L1) — a button pressed
# on its own frames after the motion produced NO special at all (measured
# by snapshot; the bare separated press did not even jab) and a single-shot rig that misses
# is a legitimate-looking zero (the #84 class).
#
# VERDICT INSTRUMENT: run guarded with GUARD_PROBE at the build's
# hitclass_map_extend body (merged-m3: 0x3ffc20, from the patch fragment —
# re-derive per build, the address moves with the allocator). SUCCESS = a
# PROBE line during a contact window; a clean run with ZERO probe lines is
# a DEAD RIG, not a pass (87's rule).
